{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475805-tc-s-oldtimers","id":1475805,"title":"TC's OldTimers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-04T16:01:51-08:00","id":1475805,"title":"TC's OldTimers","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> Aside from the big 3 (Mercer, Donighal &amp; Kaur), are there any characters in the Continuum who lived from Adventure era all the way to the Trinity era ?<br /> <br /> I seem to recall that Whitley Stiles, Mercer's prot\u00e9g\u00e9, did in 1st edition, but I'm not sure if that's still true in this one. There was also a centenarian old lady in Aberrant 1ed who erupted as a youthful nova and remembered Divis Mal from way back when.<br /> <br /> Are there characters that are canonically that old ? Or even older ? Or were there in previous editions ?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your help !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T04:01:16-08:00","id":1475832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475805-tc-s-oldtimers#post1475805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there,<br /> <br /> Aside from the big 3 (Mercer, Donighal &amp; Kaur), are there any characters in the Continuum who lived from Adventure era all the way to the Trinity era ?<br /> <br /> I seem to recall that Whitley Stiles, Mercer's prot\u00e9g\u00e9, did in 1st edition, but I'm not sure if that's still true in this one. There was also a centenarian old lady in Aberrant 1ed who erupted as a youthful nova and remembered Divis Mal from way back when.<br /> <br /> Are there characters that are canonically that old ? Or even older ? Or were there in previous editions ?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your help !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Director Thetys from Proteus was supposed to be a character known as Mechaniqu\u00e9 in Adventure era, if memory tricks me not.<br /> I think there might be others who were alive - at least as far as the Aberrant era, but would definitely have to hit the books to be sure.<br /> <br /> Anything in mind related to any such figures you have in mind? Also, there's nothing impeding you of making some of your as homages<br /> to Doc Savage, the Shadow, Fu Manchu, Indiana Jones and a bunch of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-05-2022, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T04:30:27-08:00","id":1475833,"title":"","content":"Thetis in TC, if I am not wrong, works more like a title than a name. The &quot;current&quot; Thetis in Aberrant is a old lady, but it is suggested she is not the first. I dont have the book available now, but later I will go after it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T09:51:57-08:00","id":1475843,"title":"","content":"Jake &quot;Danger Ace&quot; Stefowski from Adventure made it all the way to Aeon's 2120 setting, appearing as a holosim character named Jake Danger, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26269-bastion-avalos","name":"Bastion Avalos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T13:32:17-08:00","id":1475856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastion Avalos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475805-tc-s-oldtimers?p=1475843#post1475843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jake &quot;Danger Ace&quot; Stefowski from Adventure made it all the way to Aeon's 2120 setting, appearing as a holosim character named Jake Danger, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jake Danger: Aberrant Hunter, which points to the living Jake making it at least to the Aberrant War, if not longer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T17:12:47-08:00","id":1475866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475805-tc-s-oldtimers?p=1475832#post1475832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything in mind related to any such figures you have in mind? Also, there's nothing impeding you of making some of your as homages to Doc Savage, the Shadow, Fu Manchu, Indiana Jones and a bunch of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about doing homages or looking for anything specific. It's more that ever-plotting elders and their multi-layered conflicts and alliances provide plenty of possibilities for storylines, whether it's as patrons, plot points, or adversaries. <br /> <br /> I figure aside from possibly a long-lived stalwart, eximorphs are mostly out since they evolve beyond humanity way too fast to hang around for centuries, but there could be ancient psiads/mesmerists and ancient paramorphs alive and kicking and busy plotting to make sure their plans come to fruition, like a former medieval monk with proto-CS visions and proto-VK miracle healing who grew jaded with the passing of time and turned into a mad scholar trying to find through science the fundamental truths that his faith couldn't deliver, or an ancient talent from Byzantium who excels as an immortal power behind everchanging thrones. Each of them occasionally showing up tipping scales in one direction or another and therefore something for player characters to interact with and account for whenever they try to achieve something significant both to themselves and to one of these elders. <br /> <br /> I know I can create my own ancients, but I wondered which ones are already canon, in this edition or the previous ones. It makes integrating the stories they generate easier in the TC and keeps such long-lived characters rare, as they're meant to be fuel for stories, but shouldn't overshadow the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T20:20:20-08:00","id":1475874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475805-tc-s-oldtimers?p=1475832#post1475832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Director Thetys from Proteus was supposed to be a character known as Mechaniqu\u00e9 in Adventure era, if memory tricks me not.<br /> I think there might be others who were alive - at least as far as the Aberrant era, but would definitely have to hit the books to be sure.<br /> <br /> Anything in mind related to any such figures you have in mind? Also, there's nothing impeding you of making some of your as homages<br /> to Doc Savage, the Shadow, Fu Manchu, Indiana Jones and a bunch of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thetis was supposed to be the Machinatrix? That\u2019s news to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T11:21:48-08:00","id":1475920,"title":"","content":"Jake &quot;Danger Ace&quot; Stefokowski did indeed make it to at least the Aberrant War, under the name &quot;Jake Danger.&quot; His abilities clearly kept him spry, given that in 2062 he'd be 157 years old.<br /> <br /> It's unknown if he made it to the \u00c6on era: there's a <i>Jake Danger: Aberrant Hunter</i> TV series &quot;inspired&quot; by him, but he's played by an actor named Ellis Anson. Of course both Ellis Anson and Jake Stefokowski were portrayed by WWer Matt Milberger, so Anson is either a lookalike, a body model for a Jake Danger deepfake, or actually a 218-year-old Jake himself operating under a pseudonym.<br /> <br /> The Mechaniatrix was not intended to be Thetis to the best of my knowledge. The only connection the Mechanatrix has to the later \u00c6on era is one I invented myself, although I'm not sure if I was simply discovering something put in by <i>someone</i> on the original dev team: one of the original taint diseases was called &quot;Wexler's Disease.&quot; The Machinatrix is, of course, Hephaestia Geary-Wexler.<br /> <br /> And yes, Whitley Styles originally lasted well into the \u00c6on era. We have yet to say anything about how long he lives this time around, although he exists at least into the late 60s, when he created the Neptune Foundation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T14:05:38-08:00","id":1475937,"title":"","content":"Thanks ! All right, so to sum up, in current TC canon : Big 3, Danger Ace, and possibly Whitley Styles, but we'll have to wait for further TC releases to be sure. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475805-tc-s-oldtimers?p=1475920#post1475920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only connection the Mechanatrix has to the later \u00c6on era is one I invented myself, although I'm not sure if I was simply discovering something put in by <i>someone</i> on the original dev team: one of the original taint diseases was called &quot;Wexler's Disease.&quot; The Machinatrix is, of course, Hephaestia Geary-Wexler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat Easter egg, and actually just the sort of story hook I was looking for. If she was still around to study taint diseases and name one after herself when she discovered it, she might still be around in the Aeon era. (I guess her &quot;Sanguine Prometheus&quot; proto-nanobots kept her young.) And as a darkstar sphinx, and given her very flexible morality, she'd be great as driving force for the Transcendent Alliance throughout the centuries, still trying to figure out how, as a stalwart, to safely acquire a nova's quantum divinity without devolving into madness and body horror the way most novas did.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T17:13:43-08:00","id":1475953,"title":"","content":"This is the sidebar Stew Wilson wrote for the aborted fan-made Trinity Storytellers Handbook back in ~2003:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trinity Storytellers Handbook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Subject: Wexler's Disease<br /> From: Choi Sun-Mi, Office of Noetic Security<br /> To: Jun Shan, \u00c6on Trinity, Neptune Division<br /> Encryption: DSE<br /> Transmission type: Textfile<br /> Date: 13:21:12 12.14.2121<br /> Agent Shan, I believe it only fair to inform you that we have completed our investigation into the recent outbreak of Wexler's Disease among the people of Xinjiang. Going by the taint-ridden sample of black sludge you managed to extract from one of the victims, we were able to piece together the spread of the disease. This lead us to an underground storage facility that was being used by a minor drug ring. There were a number of crates of strange machinery, including one full of a similar black sludge in canisters. All of these crates were labeled \u201cMetachinery.\u201d We analyzed the substance in these canisters and believe that they contain active nanotechnological agents. A sample is on its way to a secure \u00c6on holding facility and the remainder will be destroyed in line with Aberrant technology protocols.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}